# Force LF regardless of the checking-out machine's core.autocrlf. Without
# this, a Windows runner (git's autocrlf default) checks text files out as
# CRLF, and this repo has byte-comparison checks that would call a
# byte-identical file "behind" for a reason nobody can fix by regenerating it:
# scripts/settings-doc.mjs's --check (docs/settings.md against package.json,
# gated in test/manifest.test.ts) and the settings-editor manifest tests that
# diff generated markdown against the committed doc. This line is what keeps
# every checkout, on every platform, the same bytes those checks compare.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.vsix binary
